    "produced_at": "2026-07-05",
    "note": "Register of the WRD red/blue flood-line sheets covering the 6 MMR rivers (41 of 494 statewide); the sheets themselves are scanned PDF maps, not digitised geometry - this file records what exists, per river, with the legal meaning of the two lines. gaps_note carries the honest-gaps record."
  },
  "place_id": "mumbai",
  "updated": "2026-07-05",
  "title": "Official flood lines (red and blue), MMR rivers",
  "intro": "The Maharashtra Water Resources Department publishes the legal flood boundaries for the region's rivers as 'red and blue line' maps. The blue line marks the 25-year flood level - construction inside it is prohibited; the red line marks the 100-year level - development between the lines is restricted. These are the lines a building permission near a river is judged against, which makes each sheet an accountability document, not just a hazard map.",
  "source": {
    "label": "WRD Maharashtra, Flood Line Maps (494 sheets statewide)",
    "url": "https://wrd.maharashtra.gov.in/Site/1315/Flood-Line-Maps"
  },
  "gaps_note": "Mumbai's own city rivers - the Mithi, Dahisar, Poisar and Oshiwara - do not appear on WRD's list: inside BMC limits flood-line demarcation sits with the corporation, and no equivalent public maps are known to exist for them. The sheets are large scanned plots (A0, 2-4 MB) and are not georeferenced.",
